@page "/website-chat"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Live chat for your website";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Live chat for your website that rings your whole team, a contact form that opens tickets, and screen sharing in a browser with nothing installed.";
    ViewData["Keywords"] = "live chat for website, website live chat, live chat South Africa, contact form, screen sharing in browser";
}
<section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h1>Live chat for your website, and browser support</h1>
        <p class="lede">Three ways for somebody who is not yet a customer — or has nothing installed — to reach you, all answered by people,
            all ending up as tickets.</p>
        <div class="next-links"><partial name="_SiteCta" /></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="facts">
            <div class="card fact"><h3>Chat on your website</h3><p>One line on your website adds a chat bubble. A visitor gives a name and an email or phone number, and everybody signed in hears it ring; the first to reply takes it. Outside your hours, or with nobody in, it becomes a ticket.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>A contact form</h3><p>A form for your website whose messages open tickets — linked to the client when we know them — with an automatic reply that gives them the ticket number.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>Screen sharing in a browser</h3><p>Your own support page where somebody can ask for help and share their screen from a browser, with nothing installed — view only, with talking if they allow it.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>Your hours, your switch</h3><p>Each one is switched on and given its hours in your portal. Nothing is on until you turn it on.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="next-links"><a class="btn" href="/remote-support">Remote support</a> <a class="btn" href="/ticketing">Ticketing</a></div>
    </div>
</section>
